{"title":"Preface","markdown":{"headingText":"Preface","headingAttr":{"id":"","classes":["unnumbered"],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\nThis reader accompanies the lecture **Supply Chain Management (SCM)** at Hochschule RheinMain, taught in the 3rd semester of the Bachelor program.\n\n## Course Philosophy\n\nSupply chain management sits at the intersection of strategy, operations, and quantitative modeling. This course takes a deliberate dual approach:\n\n-   **Quantitative rigor**: We formulate mathematical models, derive analytical solutions, and implement algorithms in R. Understanding the math is not optional — it is the foundation for sound management decisions.\n-   **Management relevance**: Every model has a story. We always ask: *What does this solution mean for the manager?* *What are the limits of the model?* *What happens when assumptions break down?*\n\n## How to Use This Reader\n\nEach chapter corresponds to one lecture module. You will find:\n\n-   **Conceptual explanations** with examples from practice\n-   **Mathematical formulations** in clean notation\n-   **R code** implementing models and visualizations — all code is reproducible\n-   **Exercises** at the end of each chapter for practice\n-   **Further reading** pointers to Chopra & Meindl chapters\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n-   Basic linear algebra and probability theory\n-   Introductory R programming (or willingness to learn)\n-   First-semester microeconomics (optimization concepts)\n\n## Main Textbook\n\nChopra, S., & Meindl, P. (latest edition). *Supply Chain Management: Strategy, Planning, and Operation*. Pearson.\n\nSupplementary:\n\n-   Silver, E., Pyke, D., & Thomas, D. — *Inventory and Production Management in Supply Chains* (CRC Press)\n-   Simchi-Levi, D. — *Operations Rules* (MIT Press)\n-   Thonemann, U. — *Operations Management* (Pearson Studium)\n\n## Software\n\nAll R code in this reader uses:\n\n``` r\nlibrary(tidyverse)        # data wrangling and visualization\nlibrary(lpSolve)          # linear and transportation problems\nlibrary(ompr)             # MILP modeling (DIY algebraic modeling)\nlibrary(ompr.roi)         # solver interface\nlibrary(ROI.plugin.glpk)  # GLPK solver\nlibrary(plotly)           # interactive visualizations\nlibrary(kableExtra)       # formatted tables\n```\n\nInstall with:\n\n``` r\ninstall.packages(c(\"tidyverse\", \"lpSolve\", \"ompr\", \"ompr.roi\",\n                   \"ROI.plugin.glpk\", \"plotly\", \"kableExtra\"))\n```\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":false,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"message":false,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"center","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":true,"code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":true,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","toc":true,"toc-depth":3,"number-sections":true,"highlight-style":"github","css":["custom.css"],"output-f